Author: sotc-pc-port <sotc-pc-port@noreply.invalid>
Date:   Thu Oct 8 14:05:53 2026 +0000

    Wave64: treat lanes beyond a small workgroup as missing on 64-lane hosts too
    
    A 32-thread workgroup leaves lanes 32-63 of the guest's 64-lane wave without
    an invocation. GCN code still reads lane 32 to merge the halves of a
    cross-lane reduction; broadcasting from it is undefined in Vulkan. The
    identity substitution from the SotC 0.2.8 build only ran for hosts with
    32-lane subgroups, so on AMD (64) Shadow of the Colossus computed garbage
    light probe coefficients: randomly tinted characters and particles.
    
    Also enables VK_KHR_shader_maximal_reconvergence for compute shaders, and
    adds buffer diagnostics (SOTC_BUFLOG).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

